# Auto-push to GitHub

After completing any code changes in this repo:

1. Run `git status` — if there are changes, commit and push.
2. Commit message: short sentence describing **why**.
3. Never commit `.env`, credentials, `*.db`, or secrets.
4. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push origin HEAD`).
5. Do this at the end of every implementation turn without asking first.

If push fails, report the error and retry once.
